// M1 — Marketing and generative AI — Session 4. Launch plan and pitch
// Numerical answers: break-even volume = fixed costs / (price − unit variable cost), rounded up.
$CATEGORY: Master/Marketing/4. Launch plan

::Contribution margin::A pair of shoes sells for 120 € and its unit variable cost is 70 €. What is the unit contribution margin, in euros?{#50}

::Break-even volume::Fixed costs for the first year are 300 000 €. Each pair sells for 120 € and its unit variable cost is 70 €. How many pairs must be sold to break even?{#6000}

::Costlier materials::Same data (fixed costs 300 000 €, price 120 €), but the recycled materials raise the unit variable cost by 15 %, from 70 € to 80.50 €. How many pairs must now be sold to break even (rounded up to a whole pair)?{#7595}

::Sell-through rate::What does the sell-through rate measure?{=The share of units received by retailers that were sold to consumers over a period ~The share of visitors who open a newsletter ~The number of shops that list the product ~The share of customers who return the product}

::Discount at launch::A brand with a premium positioning launches its new shoes with heavy discounts. What is the main risk?{=Contradicting the premium positioning and lowering the perceived value ~Increasing the perceived quality ~Reducing the number of buyers ~Breaching EU rules on environmental claims}

::New customers::Which KPI best shows whether the launch attracts new customers to the brand?{=The share of buyers who had never bought from the brand before ~The number of likes on the launch post ~The return rate ~The number of shops visited by the sales team}
